    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "64447dddc26047739c0df2c38dcbf991",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "aa91cceb661b4ecdaed8bb72ea330759"
      },
      "name": "AD-01 - Authenticate User",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-01 (Authenticate User).\nShows the workflow through which a MedAccess user (Patient/Caregiver, Pharmacist, Pharmacy Staff, or Administrator) authenticates and is granted access to role-appropriate functionality.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The user has an account where authentication is required.\n2. The MedAccess authentication service is available.\n\nPostconditions (success): The user is authenticated, a session is established, the user's role/permissions are identified, and the user is allowed to access authorized functionality.\nPostconditions (unsuccessful): The user remains unauthenticated and protected functionality remains inaccessible.\n\nModeling rules: Authentication (who the user is) is kept conceptually separate from role/permission identification (what the user may access). Invalid credentials must not reach protected functionality. This diagram does not model implementation details (databases, password hashing, JWT/tokens, APIs, specific auth providers) and does not duplicate role-specific workflows, which are represented in their own activity diagrams.\n\nTraceability: AD-01 -> UC-01 - Authenticate User.",
